# Working audit instruments: anything that records a check and its verdict for
# the authors rather than a result for a reader. The manuscript's availability
# statement points readers at this repository, so a tracked file is published
# and read as part of the submission. One ignored directory rather than
# one line per report, so an instrument written next week is covered without
# anybody editing this file.
/_internal/

# Record-level tables derived from the AI Hub corpus: its labels, boxes and keypoints,
# and the estimated-pose table that carries the keypoint labels beside the estimates.
# The AI Hub usage policy bars providing the data to others without approval, so each
# clone regenerates them from its own copy of the corpus (src/preprocess/, README.md).
/data/aihub/

# The corpus builder's own distribution files (the dataset guide and the
# labelling manual) and the publisher's LaTeX template. Redistributing them is
# theirs to license, not ours. What the analysis reads off them is stated in the
# dataset section, and nothing under src/ opens them. Obtain them from the AI Hub
# portal entry for the Artificial Intelligence Data for Preventing
# Musculoskeletal Burden Factors in Manufacturing Workers dataset.
docs/
els-cas-templates.zip
